### Spawning a subprocess with child_process.spawn() in CommonJS

Source: https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/doc/api/child_process.md

Spawns a subprocess asynchronously using CommonJS syntax and listens to stdout, stderr, and close events. Ensure stdout/stderr streams are consumed or ignored with stdio options to avoid pipe buffer blocking.

```cjs
const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');
const ls = spawn('ls', ['-lh', '/usr']);

ls.stdout.on('data', (data) => {
  console.log(`stdout: ${data}`);
});

ls.stderr.on('data', (data) => {
  console.error(`stderr: ${data}`);
});

ls.on('close', (code) => {
  console.log(`child process exited with code ${code}`);
});
```
